harge.\n\n'Wolkom by Frys-IX'", "proto_unicast": true, "proto_multicast": false, "proto_ipv6": true, "website": "http://www.frys-IX.net", "social_media": [{"service": "linkedin", "identifier": "Frys-IX"}, {"service": "website", "identifier": "http://www.frys-IX.net"}], "url_stats": "https://ixpmanager.frys-ix.net/nikhef/48hours.png", "tech_email": "noc@frys-ix.net", "tech_phone": "+31516237000", "policy_email": "noc@frys-ix.net", "policy_phone": "", "sales_phone": "", "sales_email": "", "net_count": 336, "fac_count": 15, "ixf_net_count": 338, "ixf_last_import": "2026-11-23T00:18:16Z", "ixf_import_request": "2025-09-16T06:59:08Z", "ixf_import_request_status": "finished", "service_level": "Not Disclosed", "terms": "Not Disclosed", "status_dashboard": "", "logo": null, "created": "2021-05-09T14:09:21Z", "updated": "2025-01-18T21:09:47Z", "status": "ok"}, {"id": 3789, "org_id": 38853, "name": "ERA-IX Amsterdam", "aka": "", "name_long": "ERA-IX Amsterdam", "city": "Amsterdam", "country": "NL", "region_continent": "Europe", "media": "Ethernet", "notes": "A new era of peering!\n\nThe future of peering on internet exchanges is under pressure, due to ever-growing costs, high number of failures, and a \"too corporate\" culture. In mid-2022 two internet pioneers decided to bring a better and more cost-effective alternative, and we never looked back.\n\n### Our mission\nIt is our mission to redefine peering, by offering an innovative and cost-effective IXP ecosystem. The current state of peering is not-so-great and in a headlock by large corporate IXP-operators.\n\n### Our way\nWe are truly neutral, fully privately owned and funded. Powered by a new generation of internet pioneers, our goal is to offer transparent and enterprise-ready connectivity services with a human touch.\n\n### About us\nWe are the new-generation connectivity partner, fully privately owned and funded. We have built a next-generation connectivity fabric across major datacenters in Amsterdam and Frankfurt. [